    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 1c3420476d27afea2441841fd0c5f2719bbca867 -->\n**Ready for the maintainer to merge.**\n\n**What looks good**\n- AGENTS.md matches the \"What to change\" list of #1424: start condition checked once at release step 1, start time and the (empty) P1/P2 list recorded in the release PR body, late P1/P2 not restarting or entering the cut, named under \"Known issues\" (notes and release PR comment), fixed after the tag, maintainer can still stop a cut, agents tell the maintainer of a late P1 in one line, and release-gate failures are still fixed in the cut.\n- The maintainer quote (\"We should as a rule not let P1/P2s coming in after cut - force a restart as its a ~2 hour job\") is verbatim from the issue; nothing invented.\n- No contradicting statement left: grep at the head of P1/P2 near \"cut\" in AGENTS.md, `.claude/skills/` and `.claude/agents/` finds only the two updated sentences (Priorities bullet, fix-tests sentence). The merge-ready precondition (open `release/*` PR) stays true, as the decision explains.\n- PROCESS_VERSION 54 -> 55; the decisions file follows the README format (decided, why, dropped, cost to change). Body has `Changelog: none` and the closing keyword for the issue.\n\n**Local results:** docs/process only, nothing built; mergeable with main.\n\n**Requested before merge:** none.\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n- The commit trailer names \"Claude Haiku 5.5\".\n- PR #1416 also bumps to 55; whichever merges second takes 56.\n- The issue's last bullet mentions updating the merge-ready skill text; the PR reasonably leaves it unchanged and says why.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
